# Releases & zip archives
#
# `releases/` is what the release scripts produce, and they already
# --exclude "releases/" when packaging. Nothing reads it at runtime; every copy
# under it was a frozen snapshot of an old build, five of them a stale
# serve.cjs. Keeping 1,148 files and 42 MB of that in git made every clone and
# every sync carry it. sync.sh copies the folder aside before updating and puts
# back anything the update removed, so untracking it costs nothing locally.
releases/
backups/

# Dependencies
node_modules/
node_modules_mac/
**/node_modules/
**/node_modules_mac/
venv/
__pycache__/

# The image-to-video installer's record of this machine's install.
#
# Both files were tracked, so two things that a checkout must never do
# happened: every clone inherited a "ready" record pointing at another
# computer's python, and an install on this machine dirtied two tracked
# files that the next update then refused to merge over. The app writes
# them during installation and reads them tolerantly (missing means
# "not installed here"), so nothing is lost by keeping them out of git.
# sync.sh carries a user's local copy through the transition.
app/runtimes/image-to-video/installed.json
app/runtimes/image-to-video/install-status.json

# Outputs, caches & logs
app/outputs/
app/cache/
app/tts-outputs/
app/transcriptions/
app/chat-history/
runtime-logs/
*.log
*.pid

# System & OS files
.DS_Store
.aider*
.env

# Agent skill shortcuts created by Streamlit inside the repo
.agents/
.claude/

# Everything the app writes about this machine.
#
# LUKE AI STUDIO runs from a git checkout on the user's own disk, so any file
# the app rewrites while it is used has to sit outside git. Tracking one is not
# a tidiness problem: the app changes it, and the next update that touches it is
# refused with
#
#   error: Your local changes to the following files would be overwritten by
#   merge
#
# while `git checkout -- <file>` cannot clear it, because
# scripts/setup/git-local-state.sh marks these paths skip-worktree and git will
# not match a skip-worktree pathspec. The app creates every one of these on
# first use, and all 119 validation suites pass with the folder empty, so
# nothing is lost by keeping the whole directory out of git.
#
# This is anchored at the repository root.
app/runtime-state/

# macOS metadata and local workspace junk
.fseventsd/
.Spotlight-V100/
.TemporaryItems/
.Trashes/
._*
*.orig
*.rej
*.backup
*.tmp-*
thai-tts.patch*
SuperTrader/




